    <statement><p>A rod with uniform density (mass/unit length) <m>\delta(x) = 2+\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m> 
lies on the <m>x</m>-axis
between <m>x= 0</m> and <m>x= \pi.</m>  Find the mass and center of
mass of the rod.</p>
<p>mass = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>center of mass = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2+2\pi </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi }{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>m = \int_0^\pi\,2+\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\,dx = 8.28319.</me>

The center of mass is 
<me>\overline x = \frac{\int_0^\pi\,x(2+\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right))\,dx}{8.28319} = \frac{\pi}2.</me>



</solution>
